        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e3744ca3-2bdb-5af5-9567-267627cd63c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim McIlrath, Spike Slawson, Pete Wentz, Jay Jancetic, Daniel Binaei, Adam Bishop, Timothy Miller\n- Organizations: Arma Angelus, Rise Against, Fall Out Boy, Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, Uke-Hunt, Holy Roman Empire, Harm's Way, Racetraitor, Last Action Zeros\n- Places: Chicago, Mission Viejo, California, Scottsdale, Arizona\n- Products: Where Sleeplessness Is Rest from Nightmares\n- Topics: punk rock, metalcore\n\nFacts:\n- Tim McIlrath was born on November 3, 1978.\n- Tim McIlrath is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson has been a member of Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, and Uke-Hunt.\n- Arma Angelus was a Chicago metalcore band.\n- Arma Angelus included Pete Wentz on vocals, Tim McIlrath on bass guitar, Jay Jancetic on guitar, Daniel Binaei on guitar, Adam Bishop on guitar, and Timothy Miller on drums.\n- Pete Wentz later became the bass guitarist and a backing vocalist in Fall Out Boy.\n- Tim McIlrath later became the lead singer of Rise Against.\n- Jay Jancetic later played guitar for Holy Roman Empire and Harm's Way in Chicago.\n- Daniel Binaei was formerly of Racetraitor.\n- Adam Bishop later became an English teacher at Mission Viejo High School in Mission Viejo, California.\n- Timothy Miller later played drums for the Arizona-based punk band Last Action Zeros and later became the owner of Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing in Scottsdale, Arizona.\n- Where Sleeplessness Is Rest from Nightmares is the only studio album by Arma Angelus.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
